The code statements that lead to the bug are:
if (!pci_bus_trylock(dev->subordinate)) {
    pci_dev_unlock(dev);
    goto unlock;
}
Reason:
After commit a4e772898f8b, the bridge device lock (pci_dev_trylock(dev)) is no longer taken before this point, so pci_dev_unlock(dev) unlocks a lock that was never acquired, causing lock imbalance, leading to warnings or incorrect unlocks.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (!pci_bus_trylock(dev->subordinate))
    goto unlock;
Reason:
Removing the redundant pci_dev_unlock(dev) call corrects the error handling by not attempting to unlock a lock that is not held. The pci_bus_trylock now handles the bridge lock internally, so no separate unlock is needed.

